From 6bb05ff462aead3469ce8bad0d3d44e8df82c8cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:35:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Refresh full moves each turn; never reuse piece ids

- process_turn only reset moves_left when it was <= 0, so a unit that
  ended a turn with unspent moves started the next one short. Every unit
  now gets its full allowance at the start of each turn.
- New piece ids were max(id in self.pieces) + 1, which ignores pieces
  riding in cargo, so a unit built while the highest ids were in a hold
  could duplicate a cargo id. Ids now come from a persisted counter
  (Game::next_id, serde default for old saves) that is also kept above
  every id in play, cargo included, and is never reused after a death.

Adds three regression tests; all fail on the old code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GTdH6hWDgnKLdVJLxfpadu
---
 src/game.rs       | 26 +++++++++++++---
 src/game_tests.rs | 77 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 98 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/game.rs b/src/game.rs
